From e3928bae3d40dcc27e246041c086bfb934a00456 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:40:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Exercise Desktop write invalidation across preload
 and IPC

Replace the comment-sensitive wiring substring assertion with behavioral
coverage of the real HermesGateway sender, whole transpiled preload, actual
main.ts IPC registration and real ReadCoalescer. Only Electron transport and
unrelated app bootstrap are isolated; main registration is selected from
executable AST statements, so a commented-out line cannot register a handler.

A held real WebSocket mutation exercises reads before, during and after the
write on two backends, including shared reads within each generation, a read
RPC negative control, and both success and rejection settlement.

Proof: 100 focused tests pass without skips; all src/api tests pass (44 files,
271 tests); renderer tsc and eslint pass; scripts/check reports 20 checks OK.
Both original PR2708 survivors (main handler and preload property commented
out with strings intact) now fail both cases with 2 vs 4 transport calls.
Removing either the start or settle notice also fails both cases. All four
mutants restored after testing. No production or updater changes.

Cause: source-text assertions confused retained comments with executable IPC
wiring; isolated client/coalescer tests did not compose the missing bridge.
